ke  tengoyama tells her that her dad  is probably watching intently to see  what becomes of his daughter  and his country at that point we get a  visual of the flying island in the air  and the fact that there's a giant skull  on top of it only adds to a sense of  impending doom oda definitely did a good  job with the juxtaposition between the  clear sky of the festival and the  close-up of kaido's moving castle i  really enjoy how  manga can make use of visual language in  this way just like you might see when  you're watching a movie we jump inside  the castle and go loving cipher pole  dude remarks how our straw hats and  friends refused to surrender despite the  loss of straw hat luffy i don't know how  everyone feels about this dude's go  metaphors but  i enjoy them a lot as he mentions 5 000  soldiers are no longer able to battle so  the forces should  be 24 000 kaido men to 3 000 luffy men  but pleasure and waiters on the live  floor turned against queen and when you  account for the four thousand of them  the total is twenty thousand kaido men  versus seven thousand luffy men  and as the title alludes to tama is the  key to turning more fighters to luffy's  side  so we can assume that the disparity  between the all-important  white and black go pieces will continue  to shrink  right now despite kaido beating luffy  the overall numbers are more favorable  to luffy's side than they were at the  beginning  this is how amazing the straw hats are  even if luffy and zoro are incapacitated  for the time being  they are able to not only stay in the  game but to continue to shrink the  difference in manpower it's absolutely  astonishing and truly highlights how  important a good crew  and good allies are the go metaphor is  so significant because  one piece and i'm not referring to the  title of the series here can't possibly  win  in go and one piece and this time i am  referring to the title of the series  unlike many others shonen for now at  least has done a good job  of showing that one overpowered  individual doesn't win wars but a strong  united army  that's something i really appreciate  about this series and i hope that oda  keeps it that way for as long as  possible if not forever  anyways cypherpol go dude calls the fact  that straw hat forces are doing so well  an  unexpected turn of events and yeah it  totally is and it's  why the straw hats as a whole are  legends being able to thrive against the  yonko's crew  even without the help of their captain  temporarily we then jump to the news  that momo has fallen too  as we saw last chapter unlike us they  assume this means that momo is done for  and now they think the samurai will lose  their resolve but as we saw with luffy  if you don't have the body as proof  these fighters won't fall for any tricks  that easily we then jump to the arguable  mvp trio of this chapter nami usop and  tama  they're running and nami's weather  weapon is talking as i mentioned last  time  seems zeus somehow made his way into it  and now we'll get more info about that  although nami temporarily jokes that  she's even more of a genius for creating  a talking weapon  zeus explains that it's him the one they  used to call zeus  when nami extended her weapon as he was  being eaten  it ended up absorbing his essence so to  speak the team up i wanted  so badly is here and we got it in an  even better way where now nami  is not just using something big mom  created but we get this new unique spin  on zeus which still serves to maximize  the effectiveness of nami's own weapon  i could not be happier with this turn of  events and although nami  jokes she didn't sign up for an annoying  sentient weapon  zeus did have that opportunity to prove  himself when he thought he really would  die  so i don't think it'll be too hard for  nami to forgive him for earlier events  where he turned against her  then right as bao huang is about to  announce momo's death  in order to try to lower samurai morale  she is interrupted by the appearance of  our straw hats  usopp then gets headbutted by none other  than ulti  man is this dino girl tough she's gotten  up  after the damage big mom dished out ulti  as if she didn't learn her lesson  again lays her hands on tama blaming her  for converting her  allies to the straw hat side even big  mom  nami tells her again to keep her hands  off tama  and then we start to see what the new  zeus is capable of  he turns into a kind of giant morning  star and slams into ulti  letting nami know she can use her usual  tact and zeus is just here to help with  cool new super powers  nami straight up says it's unbelievable  and this is a real  game changer nami way back in the  beginning wasn't really a fighter but  she's  become more and more of one as the story  went on and now with the amplification  of her zeus possessed weapon she's truly  become a fearsome fighter and i  love to see it happening zeus can even  share important info  like that ulti skin is crazy hard but  her insides must be messed up after big  mom's attack so she'll go  down with one strike of a thunderbolt  with his appearance  his wisdom and his power in this fight i  gotta give  zeus the mvp for this chapter but it's  the team effort that really shines here  nami can't use a thunderbolt attack  because it would hurt  tama too so usop launches an attack that  separates ulti from tama giving nami and  zeus the opening they need to launch  their attack  we then get probably the most hilarious  part in this chapter where  zeus emerges from the weapon as the  cloud we're used to seeing  nami calls out zeus but he says not  anymore  this is a new beginning and he asks for  a new name and nami in the heat of  battle suggests  cotton and then we just jumped to zeus  saying and i quote  i am zeus nami's right hand man brace  yourself end quote so  i'm happy to see that the name zeus will  stick because it's awesome but i'm so  glad  we got that scene nami's suggestion was  so bad  zeus didn't even address it and dropped  the idea of getting a new name  altogether  man i can't get enough of this dynamic  between these two  then we get another epic moment where  the huge thunderbolt  attack misses and ulti thinks it's over  she thinks she's won  but then zeus just hones in on her and  hits her anyways  now even a missed attack can be  redirected by zeus until it hits the  target  amazing stuff this seems to finally take  care of ulti  and having nami beat ulti even though  ulti was hurt already and even though  she had to rely on zeus is  so awesome people nami just beat a  flying  six member bao huang sees this and  instead of hurting our side's morale  she helps it big time by accident she  accidentally tells everyone that ulti  was beaten like page one  and that now two of the flying six  members have been defeated now many of  kaido's men  are nervous thinking that the straw hat  forces are backing them up into a corner  bao huang when told what's happening  even broadcasts the fact that she didn't  mean to broadcast  this suggesting to everyone that there  might be more bad news she's hiding  sasaki hush who and black maria all look  concerned and remember  drake already switched sides so only  three of the legendary flying six remain  that can't be comforting to hear for  kaido's men usop keeps being  invaluable by trapping bao huang in a  giant plant  allowing tama to use her to broadcast  herself to everyone including to all her  new animal-based followers  this speech is gonna be big but for now  we move on to kaido vs yamato a battle  yamato has been  itching to have no doubt kaido tells  yamato that luffy and momo are dead both  are definitely inaccurate statements  but it's still crazy to think how well  the straw hats are doing after kaido  seemingly took out luffy and momo even  kaido uses go  or chess-like analogies when he says you  should learn to protect your pieces to  yamato  kaido does not intend to let yamato  leave 